# Knowledge catalog (all documents)

- [computations/gross-margin-period] Gross margin for a period — Sanctioned SQL that produces the gross-margin figure for a period, per Acme's FY2026 Cost Allocation Standard (full COGS = product + fulfillment + shipping + payment fees).
- [computations/revenue-ytd] Revenue for a fiscal year — Sanctioned SQL that produces the recognized-revenue figure for a given fiscal year, per Acme's FY2026 Revenue Recognition Policy.
- [metrics/gross-margin] Gross Margin — Gross margin for a period, per Acme's FY2026 Cost Allocation Standard (product cost + inbound fulfillment + outbound shipping + payment fees).
- [metrics/gross-margin-legacy] Gross Margin (legacy, pre-FY2026) — Retired gross-margin definition that included only product cost. Preserved for historical query reproducibility. Do not use for new analyses.
- [metrics/revenue] Revenue — Recognized revenue for a period, per Acme's FY2026 revenue-recognition policy. Backed by an Attested Computation.
- [policies/margin-standard] Acme Retail — Cost Allocation & Margin Standard (FY2026) — Finance policy defining COGS composition and the standard gross-margin formula. Introduced FY2026 (superseded a legacy definition that excluded fulfillment/shipping).
- [policies/revenue-recognition] Acme Retail — Revenue Recognition Policy (FY2026) — Finance policy defining when a customer order is recognized as revenue. Reviewed annually.
- [skills/run-on-bq] Run an Attested Computation on BigQuery — Executor skill for `Attested Computation` concepts with `runtime: bigquery`. Binds declared parameters, submits the job, and returns a receipt the attester will verify.
- [tables/orders] Customer Orders — One row per completed customer order across web, mobile, and marketplace channels. The grain is the order, not the line item; per-line product detail lives in `order_lines`.

## Facets (document counts)

- status: stable=8, deprecated=1
- type: Metric=3, Attested Computation=2, Policy=2, BigQuery Table=1, Skill=1
